=== Complete Solutions

#sol-item(1, "D", dense: true)[
  Bile is made by the liver, stored in the gall bladder and released into the duodenum.
]

#sol-item(2, "B", dense: true)[
  Proteins are broken down through peptides to amino acids, which can be absorbed.
]

#sol-item(3, "A", dense: true)[
  The ileum, through its millions of villi, is the main absorbing surface.
]

#sol-item(4, "D", dense: true)[
  Brick-red is the positive result for a reducing sugar.
]

#sol-item(5, "C", dense: true)[
  Salivary amylase (ptyalin) converts starch to maltose.
]

#sol-item(6, "A", dense: true)[
  Bile contains no enzymes; it emulsifies fat and neutralises the acid from the stomach.
]

#sol-item(7, "D", dense: true)[
  Pepsin is adapted to the acid conditions of the stomach, about pH 2.
]

#sol-item(8, "A", dense: true)[
  The four classic adaptations: surface area, thin wall, blood supply, lacteal.
]

#sol-item(9, "C", dense: true)[
  Lipase breaks fat into fatty acids and glycerol.
]

#sol-item(10, "A", dense: true)[
  Biuret turns violet in the presence of protein.
]

#sol-item(11, "D", dense: true)[
  Grinding teeth with flat, ridged surfaces are the herbivore adaptation; canines are reduced or absent.
]

#sol-item(12, "B", dense: true)[
  Peristalsis is a wave of contraction behind the food bolus.
]

#sol-item(13, "A", dense: true)[
  The colon reabsorbs water and mineral salts, producing faeces.
]

#sol-item(14, "A", dense: true)[
  Pancreatic juice contains all three classes of digestive enzyme.
]

#sol-item(15, "A", dense: true)[
  Chewing, churning and emulsification are mechanical; enzyme action is chemical.
]

#sol-item(16, "B", dense: true)[
  Glycogen is the animal storage carbohydrate; it is converted back to glucose when blood sugar falls.
]

#sol-item(17, "D", dense: true)[
  The nitrogen-containing part is converted to urea and excreted by the kidneys.
]

#sol-item(18, "A", dense: true)[
  Carnivores shear flesh with an up-and-down movement; grinding requires side-to-side movement.
]

#sol-item(19, "B", dense: true)[
  Fatty acids and glycerol are too large for the capillaries, so they enter the lacteal.
]

#sol-item(20, "D", dense: true)[
  Maltase in the ileum completes the digestion of maltose to glucose.
]

#sol-item(21, "C", dense: true)[
  Fat provides about twice the energy per gram of carbohydrate or protein.
]

#sol-item(22, "B", dense: true)[
  Cellulose fibre cannot be digested, but it gives the gut muscles something to work against and prevents constipation.
]

#sol-item(23, "C", dense: true)[
  It sterilises the food and creates the pH 2 condition pepsin needs.
]

#sol-item(24, "A", dense: true)[
  Scurvy — bleeding gums and poor wound healing — is the classic vitamin C deficiency.
]

#sol-item(25, "C", dense: true)[
  All four tooth types on both jaws, 32 teeth in all, describe an omnivore such as an adult human.
]

#sol-item(26, "B", dense: true)[
  Digestion breaks food down, absorption moves it into the blood, assimilation is its use by the tissues.
]

#sol-item(27, "B", dense: true)[
  Length and folding, together with the villi, maximise the absorbing surface.
]

#sol-item(28, "D", dense: true)[
  Saliva contains amylase but not lipase; pancreatic juice contains amylase, trypsin and lipase.
]

#sol-item(29, "B", dense: true)[
  The liver still makes bile, but without storage the concentrated release that emulsifies a fatty meal is lost.
]

#sol-item(30, "B", dense: true)[
  Faeces are undigested food, so removing them is egestion, not excretion.
]

